From a6e6f8386ba9f3374101339d5a2e5847a99c08f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:16:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Personas as test cases; one select style across the admin

Dropdowns: the native arrow sat against the right edge of every admin
select (px-10), crowding text, arrow and border differently per browser.
All admin selects now share one style: no native appearance, 32px right
padding, a muted chevron that reads in both themes.

Personas: a row anywhere in the table opens the profile drawer (DataTable
gained onRowClick), and each persona carries test data:
- jobs to be done ('Right before a difficult conversation, I want to feel
  calmer quickly, so I can get through the day without snapping.')
- pain today (1-10), what they spend now, what they use instead, what
  would make them buy, objections in their own words
- the first sentence they would type into Aurelia (by age and language)
- access needs and connectivity
- three scenarios (when / does / expect): first open straight from the
  problem; their moment a week in; and one edge case chosen from who they
  are (grief, privacy, access needs, a lapse, the free limit, or a bad
  check-in), each with a pass condition.
The drawer shows Buying and Test cases; the role-play prompt includes
them. Tests cover the new fields and the phrasing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
